# ...Limits.h
is_specialized(bool)	true for all arithmetic types (i.e., those for which numeric_limits is specialized). false...for all other types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
min@@Minimum finite value. For floating types with denormalization (variable number of exponent bits): minimum positive normalized value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
CHAR_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
SCHAR_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
SHRT_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
INT_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
LONG_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
LLONG_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
FLT_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
DBL_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
LDBL_MIN|Minimum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
max|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
CHAR_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
SCHAR_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
UCHAR_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
SHRT_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
USHRT_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
INT_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
UINT_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
LONG_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
ULONG_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
LLONG_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
ULLONG_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
UINT_LEAST16_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
UINT_LEAST32_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
FLT_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
DBL_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
LDBL_MAX|Maximum finite value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
lowest()Minimum finite value. (since C++11) For integral types: the same as min. For floating-point types: implementation-dependent; generally, the negative of max.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
digits(int)	For integer types: number of non-sign bits (radix base digits) in the representation.For floating types: number of digits (in radix base) in the mantissa (equivalent to FLT_MANT_DIG, DBL_MANT_DIG or LDBL_MANT_DIG).[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
digits10(int)Number of digits (in decimal base) hat can be represented without change. Equivalent to FLT_DIG, DBL_DIG or LDBL_DIG for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
max_digits10(int)Number of digits (in decimal base) required to ensure that values that differ are always differentiated.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_signed(bool)true if type is signed.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_integer(bool)true if type is integer.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_exact(bool)true if type uses exact representations.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
radix(int)For integer types: base of the representation. For floating types: base of the exponent of the representation (equivalent to FLT_RADIX).[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
epsilon()Machine epsilon (the difference between 1 and the least value greater than 1 that is representable). Equivalent to FLT_EPSILON, DBL_EPSILON or LDBL_EPSILON for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_error() Measure of the maximum rounding error.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
min_exponent(int)Minimum negative integer value such that radix raised to (min_exponent-1) generates a normalized floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MIN_EXP, DBL_MIN_EXP or LDBL_MIN_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
min_exponent10(int)Minimum negative integer value such that 10 raised to that power generates a normalized floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MIN_10_EXP, DBL_MIN_10_EXP or LDBL_MIN_10_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
max_exponent(int)Maximum integer value such that radix raised to (max_exponent-1) generates a representable finite floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MAX_EXP, DBL_MAX_EXP or LDBL_MAX_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
max_exponent10(int)Maximum integer value such that 10 raised to that power generates a normalized finite floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MAX_10_EXP, DBL_MAX_10_EXP or LDBL_MAX_10_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_infinity(bool)true if the type has a representation for positive infinity.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_quiet_NaN(bool)true if the type has a representation for a quiet (non-signaling) Not-a-Number.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_signaling_NaN(bool)true if the type has a representation for a signaling Not-a-Number.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_denorm(float_denorm_style)Denormalized values -representations with a variable number of exponent bits-. A type may have any of the following enum values:
denorm_absent| if it does not allow denormalized values.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
denorm_present| if it allows denormalized values.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
denorm_indeterminate| if indeterminate at compile time.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_denorm_loss(bool)true if a loss of accuracy is detected as a denormalization loss, rather than an inexact result.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
infinity() Representation of positive infinity, if available.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
quiet_NaN() Representation of quiet (non-signaling) Not-a-Number, if available.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
signaling_NaN() Representation of signaling Not-a-Number, if available.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
denorm_min() Minimum positive denormalized value.For types not allowing denormalized values: same as min().[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_iec559(bool)true if the type adheres to IEC-559 / IEEE-754 standard.An IEC-559 type always has has_infinity, has_quiet_NaN and has_signaling_NaN set to true; And infinity, quiet_NaN and signaling_NaN return some non-zero value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_bounded(bool)true if the set of values represented by the type is finite.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_modulo(bool)true if the type is modulo. A type is modulo if it is possible to add two positive numbers and have a result that wraps around to a third number that is less.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
traps(bool)true if trapping is implemented for the type.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
tinyness_before(bool)true if tinyness is detected before rounding.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_style|	Rounding style. see round_.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
float_round_style|	Rounding style. see round_.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_toward_zero| if it rounds toward zero.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_to_nearest| if it rounds to the nearest representable value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_toward_infinity| if it rounds toward infinity.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_toward_neg_infinity| if it rounds toward negative infinity.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_indeterminate| if the rounding style is indeterminable at compile time.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
